'''''Cerastium pumilum''''', the '''dwarf mouse-ear'''<ref name=BSBI07>{{BSBI 2007 |accessdate=17 October 2014 }}</ref> or '''European chickweed''',<ref>{{PLANTS|id=CEPU4|taxon=Cerastium pumilum|accessdate=18 June 2016}}</ref> is an annual or biannual herbaceous plant, between {{Convert abbreviated|2 and 20|cm|4=1}} high, native to Central and western Europe. The petals of the white flowers are shorter or equally long as the sepals, and split in the middle, up to a quarter of the length. The fruit petioles stand diagonal to the stems, often bent over at their top. Flowering occurs between March and May. Rarely occurs on the seacoast.

